E014_value_in_void_return.cmm:3:5: semantic error: void function 'foo' cannot return a value
  |
3 |     return 10;
  |     ^^^^^^
what went wrong:
  The function 'foo' has no return type, so it cannot return a value.
how to fix:
  Use a bare 'return;' without a value, or declare a return type with '->
  <type>'.
      return;
